course: dictionary
lesson: 7712
title: Pterodactyl and pterosaur
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A pterodactyl is a flying reptile that lived at the time of the dinosaurs. Its wings were made of skin stretched from one very long finger. You can work out much of this from the context: «Pterosaurs, often called pterodactyls, were flying reptiles.» The word «flying» tells you what it did, and «reptiles» tells you what kind of animal it was.
explain: Look at the words «often called». They are a clue. They tell you that pterodactyl is a name people use in everyday talk, and that the more correct word is pterosaur. So a pterodactyl and a pterosaur are both the same kind of flying reptile.
explain: Context also tells you what a pterodactyl was not. The sentence says pterosaurs were «close cousins of dinosaurs but not dinosaurs». A context clue like this stops you from making a mistake. When a sentence says what something is not, read that part carefully too.
fact: A pterodactyl is a flying reptile.
fact: Pterodactyls lived at the time of the dinosaurs.
fact: The wings of a pterodactyl were made of skin stretched from a long finger.
fact: «Pterosaurs» is the general name, and «pterodactyl» is what people often call them in everyday talk.
fact: A pterodactyl was not a dinosaur and was not a bird.
exercise: «Pterosaurs, often called pterodactyls, were flying reptiles.» What is a pterodactyl? | A bird with long legs | A kind of small dinosaur that could not fly | A fish that lived in lakes | *A flying reptile from the time of the dinosaurs
exercise: A pterodactyl's wings were made of what? | Leaves from the trees | Thin sheets of metal | Feathers from its tail | *Skin stretched from a long finger
exercise: «Pterosaurs, often called pterodactyls, were flying reptiles.» What do the words «often called» tell you? | Pterosaurs are a kind of bird | *Pterodactyl is a name people often use for a pterosaur | Pterodactyls are the same thing as fish | Pterosaurs could not fly
test: Was a pterodactyl a dinosaur? | *No, it was a flying reptile, close to dinosaurs but not one | No, it lived in the sea | Yes, it was a bird | Yes, it was a dinosaur that could fly
test: In everyday talk, what is any flying reptile from that time often called? | A dinosaur | A bird | *A pterodactyl | A fossil
exam: Which is the best description of a pterodactyl? | *A flying reptile from the time of the dinosaurs, with wings of skin stretched from a long finger | A dinosaur with feathers that swam in the sea | A bird that lived in trees and sang | A fossil found in rocks, with no living animal behind it
